smart_library/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py                ✅ App entry — will include all routers
│   ├── database.py            ✅ DB connection via SQLAlchemy
│   ├── models.py              ✅ Central place for SQLAlchemy models (can split later)
│   ├── schemas.py             ✅ All Pydantic request/response models
│   ├── auth_utils.py          ✅ JWT encode/decode logic, expiry 
│   ├── routes/                
│      ├── auth.py             ✅ JWT encode, decode, token generator, expiry, etc.
│      ├── admin.py            ✅ Your endpoints: login, report, admin dashboard
│      ├── user.py             ✅ Borrow/return/search user operations
│      └── books.py            ✅ Inventory management
│   ├── crud/
│     ├── admin_crud.py        ✅ Your logic for reports, admin ops
│     ├── user_crud.py         ✅ Borrow, return, limit checks
│     └── books_crud.py        ✅ Add, update, delete, search books
├── alembic/                   ✅ Will auto-fill on `alembic init`
│   └── versions/
├── alembic.ini                ✅ Alembic config
├── requirements.txt           ✅ All team should use this for pip install
├── Dockerfile                 ✅ Later: containerize the whole app
└── docker-compose.yml         ✅ Optional: DB + API in one go


python -m venv venv...
venv\Scripts\activate
mkdir app
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip list
pip install alembic
alembic init alembic
In alembic.ini, and update this line with your PostgreSQL connection string:
sqlalchemy.url = postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/smart_library
In alembic/env.py

Find this section:
# add your model's MetaData object here
# for 'autogenerate' support
# from myapp import mymodel
# target_metadata = mymodel.Base.metadata
🔁 Replace with:
from app.database import Base  # 👈 import your Base
from app import models         # 👈 import your models
target_metadata = Base.metadata

uvicorn app.main:app --reload

